{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01M6BsKnUBKD5St8YxDbAioE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Summary â€” Deliverables session: `anchor_gui.py`\n\n**What it is**\n- `anchor_gui.py` is Anchor's primary application: a self-contained, stdlib-only Python HTTP server that serves the interactive dashboard and writes changes directly to the markdown files. Its module docstring states it \"Starts a local HTTP server that serves the interactive dashboard and provides API endpoints so that every click (done, add, capture) writes directly to the markdown files, logs changes, and refreshes the state.\"\n- The file is large and monolithic â€” **8,096 lines** (â‰ˆ394 KB) as of the 2026-06-13 build â€” holding parsing, data-gathering, change operations, HTML generation, and the HTTP handler in one module.\n\n**Paths & data layer**\n- Path constants resolve through the shared `paths` helper, honoring `ANCHOR_DATA_DIR` (unset â†’ the code dir). `ANCHOR_DIR` is the code dir (static assets); `DASHBOARD_MD`, `PROJECTS_MD`, `INBOX_MD`, `DOMAINS_DIR`, `LOGS_DIR`, `CANCELLED_MD`, `SAVED_FOR_LATER_MD` come from `_paths`.\n- A process-wide `WRITE_LOCK` (from `paths`) is held around every markdown/JSON mutation so concurrent requests under `ThreadingHTTPServer` can't lose an update. `ensure_data_dirs()` is called explicitly at startup. Errors log to `logs/errors.log` via `logging`.\n\n**Markdown read/write core**\n- Parsers read markdown into Python dicts: `parse_tasks_from_md`, `parse_projects_from_md`, `parse_inbox_from_md`, `parse_archived_tasks`; `serialize_task_line` writes them back; `gather_all()` aggregates DASHBOARD.md plus the domain files.\n- Change operations: `mark_done`, `mark_undone`, `add_task`, `capture_inbox`, `link_task`, `edit_task`, `edit_project`, `cancel_task`, `save_for_later`, `restore_task`, `log_change`, plus archive helpers (`_append_to_archive`, `_remove_task_from_files`). A `_with_write_lock` decorator wraps mutations.\n\n**R&D control surface (v2â€“v4) rendering**\n- The bulk of the file renders the R&D project surface: `render_project_window_html` (the project cockpit) spans roughly lines 1856â€“3646 â€” the single largest function. Supporting renderers include `render_project_tile_html`, `render_projects_view_html`, `_render_kanban_html`, `_render_lane_sessions`, `_render_grass_board`, `_render_effort_card`, `render_header_rollup_html`, `render_cost_rollup_html`, and `render_deliverables_html`.\n- Summary generation is triggered (not run inline on render) via `_trigger_project_summary`, `_trigger_session_summary`, and `_trigger_project_session_summaries`. Project lifecycle helpers: `create_new_folder_project`, `select_existing_project`, `discover_and_adopt`, `open_project_instance`, `_maybe_git_init`, `ensure_anchor_deliverable`.\n\n**Terminal / WebSocket substrate**\n- The module hand-rolls an RFC-6455 WebSocket codec in stdlib: `ws_accept_key`, `encode_text_frame`, `encode_close_frame`, `encode_pong_frame`, `_encode_frame`, `decode_frames` â€” used for the ConPTY terminal transport.\n- Traversal-safe static asset routes are served by `anchor_term_asset`, `xterm_asset`, and `brand_asset` (guarded by `_unsafe_path_seg`), backing the vendored anchor-term, xterm.js, and Ghost World Labs brand assets.\n- A build/cache-busting identity is computed by `_compute_build_id` and emitted via `cache_bust_script`.\n\n**HTTP server & lifecycle**\n- `generate_html(projects, tasks, inbox)` builds the full dashboard HTML (single function, ~line 4320 onward). `AnchorHandler(BaseHTTPRequestHandler)` implements the GET/POST API endpoints.\n- Single-instance enforcement: `_ExclusiveThreadingHTTPServer` and `make_server(host=\"127.0.0.1\", port=8777)` bind exclusively (the `SO_EXCLUSIVEADDRUSE` guard against the rogue-supervisor bug); `resolve_bind_host` and `main()` handle startup, and `_heartbeat_watchdog` runs a background liveness check. Default bind is loopback `127.0.0.1:8777`.\n\n**Provenance note**\n- This is an `imported`/pinned deliverable (the live application file), not a trio RUN artifact â€” so no run cost/token/wall-clock metrics are associated with it. Claims above are grounded in the file's own header, structure, and definitions rather than an execution log."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":638,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3199,"cache_read_input_tokens":49278,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3199},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41bc94d6-5e70-4f19-87da-c0a8fb19d614","uuid":"6882c5e8-4f33-4024-aff4-113a51c4279e","request_id":"req_011Cc1hYxq37LP7GzeakcC38"}
